  "content": "Gold price up by Rs 3,000 per tola\nOnlinekhabar\nSunday, October 12, 2025\n0\nComments\nKathmandu, October 12\nThe price of gold has increased by Rs 3,000 per tola (11.66 grams) today as compared to Friday.\nGold is being traded at Rs 238,000 per tola today against 235,000 on Friday, according to the Federation of Gold and Silver Dealers’ Association.\nSimilarly, the Federation has fixed the price of silver at Rs 3,125 per tola. It was traded at Rs 3,085 on Friday.\nGold is being traded at 4,016 US dollar per ounce in the international market today.\nReact to this post\nHot Topics\ngold\nnepali cricket\nflood\nSushila Karki\ninsurance\nICC T20 World Cup Qualifier\nKapan\nConversation\nNew\nOld\nPopular\nAdd Comment\nLogin to comment\nRemenber me\nForgot password?\nLogin\nNot have account yet?\nSignup Now\nOr use Social Media?\nGoogle\nFacebook\nTwitter\nForgot Password?\nSend Password Reset Link\nBack\nRelated News\nSlight drop in gold price\n2 days ago\nGold price reaches record high at Rs 235,960 per tola\n5 days ago\nGold price surges by Rs 10,000 per tola after Dashain\n6 days ago\nGold price reaches record high\n3 weeks ago\nGold price hikes by Rs 1,100 per tola\n3 weeks ago\nGold prices hit new record, rise by Rs 1,600 per tola\n1 month ago\nMost Read\nUAE introduces new rules for Visit Visa Sponsorship\n12 stranded backpackers rescued from Langtang\nWhen a joke fuels division: Casual hate speech and the Gen Z revolution in Nepal\nGold price reaches record high at Rs 235,960 per tola\nGold price surges by Rs 10,000 per tola after Dashain\nSubscribe to our newsletter\nSubscribe to Onlinekhabar English to get notified of exclusive news stories.\nEditor's Pick\nEditor's Pick\n4 government buildings, including Supreme Court, declared unfit for use\n3 weeks ago\nEditor's Pick\nCharred body found at Koteshwor Bhatbhateni, Gen-Z protest death toll rises to 74\n4 weeks ago\nEditor's Pick\nNo consensus on Hami Nepal’s claim of leading the Gen-Z movement\